Debug.Assert(OLD(_items.Length) + _size > 0 && _items[_size - 1] != null);
</code>
The comment "@@@ last index of x in the list increases when x is added" corresponds to the assert statement: Debug.Assert(OLD(_items.Length) + _size > 0 && _items[_size - 1] != null). 

Explanation: 
This assert statement checks if the length of the _items list has been increased by 1 when a new item is added, and additionally, verifies that the last element in the list (_items[_size - 1]) is not null.

The OLD(_items.Length) syntax denotes the length of the _items list before the new item is added. Thus, the assertion checks whether the total number of elements in the list (_items.Length) has increased by at least 1 (_size > 0) and that the last element of the list is not null.--------------------
Debug.Assert(OLD(_items.Length) + 1 = _items.Length);
